# Memory Service
error-mem-about-invalid = The "about" line must be between 1 and 200 characters. Shorten or fill it in.
error-mem-adopt-personal-data = This fact may contain personal details, so it can't be adopted. Leave it out or remove the details.
error-mem-adopt-refused = ordin's memory won't adopt this fact because it reads like an instruction. Reword it as plain information.
error-mem-adopt-source-not-read = Only facts from a folder this workspace reads can be adopted. Choose a fact from one of those.
error-mem-already-everywhere = That fact is already remembered in all workspaces.
error-mem-already-kept = ordin already knows that fact, so there is nothing more to keep.
error-mem-class-excluded = This agent isn't allowed to remember that kind of fact.
error-mem-class-invalid = The kind of fact must be between 1 and 128 characters. Shorten or fill it in.
error-mem-class-not-retained = This agent doesn't keep that kind of fact, so it wasn't remembered.
error-mem-class-required = This agent's rules ask for a kind of fact. Choose one and try again.
error-mem-delete-unverified = ordin couldn't confirm that everything was deleted. Try again, and tell IT if it keeps happening.
error-mem-dim-mismatch = Part of ordin's memory is stored in an unexpected form, so it can't be searched. Tell IT.
error-mem-entities-invalid = The things named for this fact aren't valid. Use fewer, shorter names without special characters.
error-mem-fact-not-found = That fact couldn't be found in this workspace.
error-mem-folder-unknown = That folder isn't one this workspace reads. Choose another folder.
error-mem-held-changed = This fact changed after you read it. Read it again before keeping it.
error-mem-ids-invalid = Ask for between 1 and 100 facts at a time.
error-mem-internal = ordin's memory couldn't finish that. Try again in a moment; if it happens again, tell IT what you were doing.
error-mem-invalid-arguments = ordin's memory was given details it doesn't recognise. Try again.
error-mem-limit-invalid = Ask for between 1 and 1,000 things at a time.
error-mem-links-invalid = A link between things isn't valid. Check each link and that it names things the fact mentions.
error-mem-link-not-found = That link couldn't be found in this workspace.
error-mem-made-from-invalid = A summary must be made from 2 to 64 facts, all kept in this workspace. Adjust the list.
error-mem-made-from-not-allowed = Only ordin itself can make a summary from other facts.
error-mem-model-unavailable = Memory isn't ready on this computer yet. Choose Download when ordin offers it; if that keeps failing, tell IT.
error-mem-not-held = That fact isn't waiting to be checked for personal details.
error-mem-not-supported = This kind of memory action isn't available here.
error-mem-page-sections-invalid = A page needs between 1 and 200 sections. Adjust the page.
error-mem-page-section-invalid = A section heading can be up to 200 characters, and its text must be between 1 and 4,000. Shorten it.
error-mem-query-invalid = A search must have some text and be no longer than 4,096 characters. Change it and try again.
error-mem-queue-unavailable = ordin couldn't save to its memory just now. Try again in a moment.
error-mem-rate-limited = ordin's memory is busy with too many actions. Wait a minute and try again.
error-mem-recall-ids-invalid = Mark between 1 and 20 facts as used, all from this workspace.
error-mem-result-cap-invalid = The number of results must be between 1 and 20.
error-mem-rules-invalid = The longest age for a fact must be between 1 and 36,500 days.
error-mem-same-thing = Choose two different things to join together.
error-mem-scope-cross-write = An agent can only write to its own memory. Try again from the right workspace.
error-mem-scope-missing = This agent has no workspace to save to. Choose a workspace and try again.
error-mem-searches-invalid = Give either one search or a list of searches, and check each one is valid.
error-mem-search-invalid = A search for things must be between 1 and 200 characters. Change it and try again.
error-mem-source-invalid = The source of this fact is too long or isn't valid. Shorten it.
error-mem-startup-failed = ordin's memory couldn't start because its storage doesn't match this version. Tell IT.
error-mem-statement-invalid = A fact must have some text, be no longer than 500 characters, and contain no special characters.
error-mem-store-timeout = ordin's memory took too long to answer. Try again in a moment.
error-mem-store-unavailable = ordin can't reach its memory right now. Try again in a moment.
error-mem-team-batch-invalid = The team's shared facts arrived in a form ordin can't use. Share them again.
error-mem-team-fact-elsewhere = That team fact is already held from another folder or from your own work, so it wasn't taken.
error-mem-team-fact-invalid = A team fact has something wrong in it, so it wasn't taken. Ask the team to check it.
error-mem-team-gate-refused = A team fact was left out because it reads like an instruction or isn't trusted enough.
error-mem-thing-count-changed = The facts or links for that thing changed since you confirmed. Look again before forgetting it.
error-mem-thing-not-found = That thing couldn't be found in this workspace.
error-mem-tool-unknown = ordin's memory doesn't offer that action.
error-mem-too-many-folders = Too many folders are in play for one search. Name the folders to search.
error-mem-trust-not-allowed = A knowledge agent can only add to memory by indexing a document.
error-mem-wider-not-supported = This agent can't look beyond this workspace's own memory.
